+++
title: Terms
+++

These Terms govern a client's engagement with Yomonsni ("we," "us," or
"our") for coaching services, and with any workshop or retreat offered
in connection with those services.

**1. Introductory Conversation.** Before we accept a client's first
booking, we ask that the client and their intended coach — or, in the
case of a workshop or retreat, one of the coaches hosting that event —
first speak for a complimentary, no-obligation conversation of
approximately thirty minutes. This conversation exists so that both the
client and the coach can, in good faith, confirm that the relationship
is a good fit before anything is booked, and we encourage every
prospective client to use it accordingly.

**2. Bookings and Cancellations.** Once that introductory conversation
has taken place and a booking is confirmed, the booking is final, and no
refund will be issued. We ask that a client take the introductory
conversation seriously for exactly this reason, so that a booking is
only ever made once the client feels genuinely ready to proceed.

**3. Nature of Coaching.** Coaching, as practiced here, is a process of
reflective conversation offered in support of a client's own growth and
self-discovery. Nothing in a coaching relationship obligates a client to
take any particular action, nor should anything said in a session be
understood as a directive to do so. Any action a client chooses to take
in their own life, whether during or after a coaching engagement, is
taken entirely of that client's own free will, and the client alone is
responsible for that choice and for whatever outcome, favorable or
otherwise, may follow from it. Coaching does not promise, and should not
be understood to promise, any particular result.
